# Service Policy

Optional per-user config for the service reload / restart policy.
See `rules/service-reload.md` for the full policy. Missing file =
defaults apply (reload auto-proceeds, restart asks).

Format: one service name per line under each section heading, as
a `- ` bullet. Match by systemd unit name without `.service` —
e.g. `postgresql`, not `postgresql.service`. For templated units,
use the full instance name (e.g. `nginx@default`).

## reload-always-ask

Services listed here will NOT auto-reload — Hostwarden will ask
before every `systemctl reload`. Use it for stateful services
where a bad config reload could cause real damage.

## restart-auto

Services listed here WILL auto-restart — Hostwarden will run
`systemctl restart` without asking. Use it for services that come
back up quickly and are not critical.

## restart-never

Services listed here will NOT auto-restart — Hostwarden refuses
the restart outright, without prompting; do it manually or remove
the entry. Use it for databases and anything where you want to
control every restart yourself.
